Local changes to backport: loopback host configuration; deadline-aware result
wait; finite Nx6 output validation and CPU wire tensors; base/LoRA loader with
saved-base selection and strict normalization checks; CLI serve dispatch.
The service protocol is unchanged. One client at a time; no request identifiers.

Training additions, 2026-10-27: enable_training_resume.py adds opt-in local LoRA
optimizer/scheduler/RNG saves and retains only the most recent optimizer state.
It also restores the original base path before loading an adapter-only training
checkpoint, and fails if resume adapter weights were not restored.
PriMeR19 preparation converts recorded degrees/raw encoder values into the
client's calibrated SO101 units, maps RGB camera slots, and physically isolates
train/validation because the installed LeRobot loader reads all local files.

Model weights and tokenizer retain the upstream Gemma terms. They are downloaded
separately and are not included in source backups.
